Panoptes bundles or references third-party open-source components.

Core runtime packages are declared in backend/pyproject.toml and frontend/package.json.

Planned detector artifacts:
- desklib/ai-text-detector-v1.01: Hugging Face model; verify exact model card and license before release.
- DroidDetect-Base: verify exact model card and license before release.
- C2PA tooling: verify package and specification terms before enabling non-development provenance verification.

Research datasets:
- DroidCollection: cite and follow dataset terms; do not redistribute unless permitted.
- Defactify_Text_Dataset (Rajarshi-Roy-research, Hugging Face; Roy et al. 2026, arXiv:2510.22874):
  paper CC BY 4.0; dataset repository declares no separate license. Panoptes uses it as a
  local-only bench dataset: raw text is never committed or redistributed — only SHA-256
  hashes, row counts, and fitted model parameters (datasets/manifests/defactify-text.json).
- RAID (liamdugan/raid, Hugging Face; Dugan et al. 2024, ACL, doi:10.18653/v1/2024.acl-long.674):
  MIT-licensed benchmark. Panoptes fetches the labeled train split locally only: raw text is
  never committed or redistributed — only SHA-256 hashes, row counts, and fitted parameters
  (datasets/manifests/raid.json).
- M4GT-Bench (mbzuai-nlp/M4GT-Bench, GitHub + Google Drive; Wang et al. 2024, ACL,
  doi:10.18653/v1/2024.acl-long.218): repository declares no license for the data files.
  Panoptes fetches the Subtask A JSONL files locally only: raw text is never committed or
  redistributed — only SHA-256 hashes, row counts, and fitted parameters
  (datasets/manifests/m4gt.json).
- EvoBench (happy-Moer/EvoBench, GitHub; ACL 2025 Findings, doi:10.18653/v1/2025.findings-acl.754):
  repository declares no license. Panoptes fetches the repository tarball at a pinned commit
  locally only: raw text is never committed or redistributed — only SHA-256 hashes, row counts,
  and fitted parameters (datasets/manifests/evobench.json).

External detector baseline weights (scored locally on frozen protocol splits; never redistributed):
- Falcon-7B and Falcon-7B-Instruct (tiiuae, Hugging Face; Almazrouei et al. 2023): Apache 2.0.
  Used as the Binoculars observer/performer pair (Hans et al. 2024, ICML). Weights are downloaded
  to the local Hugging Face cache only; only the resulting detection scores enter the signed
  artifact (backend/artifacts/external-baselines.json).
- GPT-J-6B (EleutherAI, Hugging Face; Wang & Komatsuzaki 2021): Apache 2.0. Used as the
  Fast-DetectGPT scoring model (Bao et al. 2024, ICLR). Weights stay in the local cache only;
  only detection scores enter the signed artifact.

The current checked-in calibration artifact is synthetic and intended only to validate the pipeline.

Contributor data policy:
- Dataset manifests under `datasets/manifests/` are pointer records, not dataset redistribution.
- Raw third-party corpora must not be committed unless their license explicitly permits redistribution and the samples are fixture-scale.
- Every new model, dataset, watermark scheme, or substantial dependency requires an entry here.
- Calibration artifacts must include a canonical SHA-256 artifact hash and reproducibility metadata.
